The viable family is the paper’s sequencing search problem in a crowded cyclic prime group. I’m using growing set size (well beyond the paper’s fixed-size 20/22/23 guarantees) and keeping the modulus only slightly larger than the set, because sparse groups make almost every permutation valid. The generator samples a rainbow modular path first, then forgets its edge order; every displayed element comes from the same process, so there is no separate “plant” versus “decoy” distribution.
